From d204ad4d7ab64d882af9edf88f5e2a390abb2da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:55:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] arm64: errata: treat the T6050 vGIC SEIS as broken,
 like T6040 and T8140

ICH_VTR_EL2 on the K116s (MacBook Pro 16-inch, M5 Pro, firmware 27.2)
reads 0x90580007 at EL2: eight list registers and SEIS set, on the boot
CPU, part 0x064. The other Apple cores with this value are listed in
apple_broken_seis_cpus so that KVM does not trust the locally generated
SError the vGIC claims to support; without the entry SMP guests livelock.
Add the two T6050 core parts.

The register was read through the boot loader's proxy at EL2 before
Linux ran. The K116s now runs Linux at EL2 on every CPU (padded Stage 1,
27.2) with this entry, which logs "Known broken GICv3 SEIS
implementation", and KVM works: qemu -accel kvm -M virt,gic-version=3
-cpu host guests with 1, 2, 6 and 18 vCPUs boot and exit cleanly.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/cpu_errata.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu_errata.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu_errata.c
index 9d7e134419fb..fa1a6a83caa9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu_errata.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu_errata.c
@@ -318,6 +318,8 @@ static const struct midr_range apple_broken_seis_cpus[] = {
 	MIDR_ALL_VERSIONS(MIDR_APPLE_TAHITI_P),
 	MIDR_ALL_VERSIONS(MIDR_APPLE_T8142_E),
 	MIDR_ALL_VERSIONS(MIDR_APPLE_T8142_P),
+	MIDR_ALL_VERSIONS(MIDR_APPLE_T6050_064),
+	MIDR_ALL_VERSIONS(MIDR_APPLE_T6050_065),
 	{},
 };
 
